killTree only signals the original process group. A descendant that calls setsid() survives, and the new wait returns immediately when the original group disappears. This leaves the requested whole-tree termination incomplete. Targeted command: bun -e 'import { strict as assert } from "node:assert"; import {runProcess} from "./src/util/proc.ts"; const r=await runProcess({cmd:["python3","-c","import os,time; p=os.fork();
if p==0:
